# aurora.local / packages/identity/pins.env.example
#
# Curated, human-reviewed image pins — the ".example" suffix mirrors the
# existing .env / .env.example convention (see .gitignore): the real
# packages/identity/pins.env is gitignored (generated by `scripts/pin.sh
# --refresh`/`--apply`, host-local), so committed curated recommendations
# live here instead. Copy or merge into packages/identity/pins.env to adopt.
#
# See dev/notes/pinnable-versions-progress.md for the full inventory and
# reasoning behind every choice in this file.
#
# Once adopted as pins.env, this is consumed by scripts/lib/render.sh
# render_pins() into the environment before `docker compose up`. It only
# takes effect in compose.yml image: lines after `scripts/pin.sh --apply`
# has rewritten them to ${IMAGE_<SVC>} — that has NOT been run, so
# compose.yml still says `image: authelia/authelia:latest`. compose.yml is
# untouched by this work; this file is the curated data, ready for that
# step when the owner chooses it.
#
# Format: repo:tag@sha256:digest (differs from scripts/pin.sh --refresh, which
# currently discards the tag — see progress log finding #2).
#
# Digests obtained with:
#   docker buildx imagetools inspect --format '{{.Manifest.Digest}}' <ref>

# authelia/authelia — latest stable release is 4.39.20, released 2026-05-26
# (~11 weeks old as of the check below, not an rc/beta; confirmed against
# the project's GitHub releases page). Verified the tag `4.39.20` exists and
# resolves to the exact same manifest-list digest as `:latest` today, i.e.
# `:latest` has not drifted ahead of it. Multi-arch: linux/amd64,
# linux/arm/v7, linux/arm64 — confirmed via `docker buildx imagetools
# inspect`; covers both the Optiplex (amd64) and a Pi (arm64). Checked
# 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_AUTHELIA=authelia/authelia:4.39.20@sha256:1b363e9279e742397966333f364e0876ae02bf5c876de73e83af6d48c57ff51b
